body:
The bug was introduced in commit 2a10291. I confirmed that `2a10291~1` doesn't have this problem, but it appears in `2a10291`.

More specifically, it's caused by the removal of the update of `moving_selection` and `moving_selection_attempt` in `AnimationTrackEdit::gui_input` where the right-click menu is built:
```
	menu->add_icon_item(get_editor_theme_icon(SNAME("Remove")), TTR("Delete Key(s)"), MENU_KEY_DELETE);
}
menu->reset_size();

// lines below are removed
moving_selection_attempt = false;
moving_selection = false;
// lines above are removed

menu->set_position(get_screen_position() + get_local_mouse_position());
```
This issue could be fixed by adding these lines back. I'm currently investigating how they affect the logic.

The bug is caused by `moving_selection_attempt` not being updated correctly. The right-click sets `moving_selection_attempt` to `true`. On our latter left-click, `mm.is_valid() && mm->get_button_mask().has_flag(MouseButtonMask::LEFT) && moving_selection_attempt` is evaluated to `true`, so the offset between two clicks is saved in `moving_selection_offset`, and a redraw based on `moving_selection_offset` is queued for the next frame.

When we click other keys, they are also redrawn based on `moving_selection_offset`, so they all shift.

For context, the right-click calls [`_try_select_at_ui_pos`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/29b945f2eb52ef8d470f23649f584f4809ef5f39/editor/animation/animation_track_editor.cpp#L3253), which sets `moving_selection_attempt` to `true`. The left-click makes [`mm.is_valid() && mm->get_button_mask().has_flag(MouseButtonMask::LEFT) && moving_selection_attempt`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/29b945f2eb52ef8d470f23649f584f4809ef5f39/editor/animation/animation_track_editor.cpp#L3396) evaluate to true, which saves the offset between two clicks in `moving_selection_offset` and emits "move_selection" signal. The signal is connected to [`AnimationTrackEditor::_move_selection`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/29b945f2eb52ef8d470f23649f584f4809ef5f39/editor/animation/animation_track_editor.cpp#L6194-L6197) which calls `_redraw_tracks`, which triggers `NOTIFICATION_DRAW` for all track_edits. And finally when drawing we [compute the screen_pos](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/29b945f2eb52ef8d470f23649f584f4809ef5f39/editor/animation/animation_track_editor.cpp#L2337-L2341) by
```cpp
if (editor->is_key_selected(track, i) && editor->is_moving_selection()) {
	time_offset += editor->get_moving_selection_offset();
}

float screen_pos = time_offset * scale + limit;
```
When we click other keys subsequently, the [`_key_selected`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/29b945f2eb52ef8d470f23649f584f4809ef5f39/editor/animation/animation_track_editor.cpp#L6153-L6173) function is called by a signal, which calls `_redraw_tracks`, which results in the same drawing logic.

To solve this we can add a `moving_selection_attempt = false` after [`bool selected = _try_select_at_ui_pos(...)`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/29b945f2eb52ef8d470f23649f584f4809ef5f39/editor/animation/animation_track_editor.cpp#L3253).
